 "observations": [
  "col_left L2: «Πατανῆς» is Greek, read at 6,000 dpi: the circumflex stands on the η, whose long right stroke is printed apart from the letter (a thin stroke from mid height to 2.4 points below the baseline, before the ς); read η. «al-Battānī» has bars over the second a and the last i (2.4 by 0.8 points). The comma after «n. 1» is printed short (1.6 by 2.2 points, its foot 0.8 point below the baseline).",
  "col_left L3: «*Pauliśa-siddhānta*» is printed with ś (an acute over the s) and a bar over the a.",
  "col_left L7: «(*watad*)» is printed in italics; the e of «una e» is printed broken, its lower part apart like a point; it is not a point. The o of «quatuor» is printed broken; read o.",
  "col_left L10: a speck (1.2 by 1.0 points) above the left side of the e after «[i.», 7.5 points above the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L12: the last o of «loco» and of «spurio» is printed broken, like ‹ ›; read o.",
  "col_left L15: «περίπατος» is Greek, with the acute on the ι.",
  "col_left L16: «*Periplus maris Erythraei*» is printed in italics. The comma after «II» is printed short (1.6 by 2.6 points, its foot 0.8 point below the baseline).",
  "col_left L22, L23: «ash-» «shāh» has a bar over the a; the upper end of the a of «shāh» stands apart from its bowl.",
  "col_left L26: «*peshḥā*» (twice) has the dot under the italic h (1.6 by 1.4–1.5 points) and a bar over the a; «*ōrganōn*» has bars over both o's and «*trayānāy*» over the second and the third a. A speck (0.8 by 0.7 point) under the first a of «*trayānāy*», 2.4–3.1 points below the baseline, is not transcribed; it is not a dot below (the dots below of this type are 1.5–1.8 points).",
  "col_left L26: the Syriac «ܦܫܚܐ» (peshḥā) is printed in Serto without vowel points, read at 5,000 dpi: pe, shin, ḥeth and a final alaph. The curve above it is the foot of a g of the line above (L25).",
  "col_left L33: «Dhū ’l qarnayn» is printed with a bar over the u, the apostrophe of elision and a space, without the hyphen that the same name has in R33; transcribed as printed.",
  "col_left L34: the 1 of «192» is printed broken, like ı.",
  "col_left L36: the s of «Byzantinus» is printed broken; a speck after «196.» is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L41: the two «x» are small capitals (the roman numeral ten), set {sc:x}.",
  "col_left L42: «al-Battānī» has bars over the second a and the last i (2.0 by 0.8 points). The italic 5 of «*65-66*» is printed broken: a piece of it (1.1 by 1.3 points) stands apart at mid height, like a hyphen at low resolution; it is not a hyphen.",
  "col_left L43, L45: the s of «seu» is printed broken, its lower terminal apart like a point; between the two italic 5s of «*55*» the ball of the first 5 stands apart (1.4 by 1.8 points), like a point. Neither is a point.",
  "col_left, col_right: in this type the ball terminals of a, r and of the figures 2, 3, 5 and 9 are joined to their letters by hairlines that often did not print; on this page such balls stand apart in many words and numbers (68 pieces in all, listed by loose_pieces.py), among them the lower balls of the 3s of «314» (L4), «238» (L44, twice) and «238-243» (R37) and the tail of the 9 of «290» (R7), which stand on the baseline like points. None of them is a point.",
  "col_right L2: several small capitals are printed broken: the lower left serif of the second X of «{sc:lxxvi}» and of the first X of «{sc:xxvii}» stands apart like a point, and the right arm of the V of «{sc:lxxvi}» and of «{sc:xxvii}» stands apart from the letter. Read as printed.",
  "col_right L5: the hyphen of «290-292» is printed short (2.3 by 1.1 points).",
